# deploy/pins.env — the single source of truth for every third-party pin the
# node-agent image lineage builds from.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Before 2026-08-20 the same four refs were declared TWICE
# in deploy/Dockerfile.vulkan (once in the build stage, once in the runtime stage
# so the provenance LABELs could interpolate them), kept in step by a Python
# guard in build-images.sh; DOCKER_VERSION and CUDA_PKG_VERSION were duplicated
# with no guard at all. Every pin is now declared exactly ONCE, at global scope
# (before the first FROM), and a bare `ARG NAME` re-declare inside a stage
# inherits the global default -- so a stage can read a pin for a LABEL without
# repeating its value. This file is what build-images.sh and CI read so the
# pins also exist outside the Dockerfile, which is what makes the toolchain
# artefact tag computable without parsing Docker syntax.
#
# FORMAT: strict KEY=VALUE, no quotes, no expansion, no comments on value lines.
# It is `source`d by bash AND parsed by CI with plain `grep`/`cut`, so keep it
# boring. Every KEY here must be a declared ARG in deploy/Dockerfile.vulkan --
# build-images.sh asserts that and refuses to build otherwise.
#
# CHANGING A PIN. Edit here only. The Dockerfile's global ARG defaults are
# asserted to agree with this file on every build (build-images.sh
# check_pins_agree), so a change in one place and not the other is a hard build
# failure rather than a silent drift. Prose rationale for each pin stays in
# docs/third-party-pins.md and in the Dockerfile comment at the point of use.
#
# TOOLCHAIN KEYS vs RUNTIME KEYS. The keys marked TOOLCHAIN below feed the
# quasar-gst-toolchain artefact tag (deploy/toolchain-hash.sh); changing any of them
# means a new toolchain must be compiled. The others are consumed by the runtime
# stages only, so changing them costs a ~5-minute image build, not a ~40-minute
# toolchain build. Do not move a key between the two groups without updating
# deploy/toolchain-hash.sh.

# ── TOOLCHAIN pins (change ⇒ the ~40 min GStreamer toolchain is rebuilt) ──────

# Fedora 43 base from quasar-images. F43 (not F42) because the Vulkan
# video-encode extension needs vulkan-headers >= 1.4.317; F42 ships 1.4.313.
QUASAR_BASE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/accreleus/quasar-base:latest

# Patched GStreamer. 1.28 is the first release carrying vulkanh264enc.
GST_VERSION=1.28.4

# gst-plugins-rs `rtp` plugin -> rtpgccbwe (ABR bandwidth estimation). The 0.15
# BRANCH is moving, so this is the exact SHA (0.15.3-cee4522) baked into the
# known-good image. 0.15 pairs with GStreamer 1.28; 0.13/0.14 will not build.
GST_PLUGINS_RS_REF=cee45224cb2d10e1523af4f256d0dd64c8b29491

# gst-interpipe, games-on-whales fork -> the launcher<->game swap boundary.
GST_INTERPIPE_REF=0c454917

# gst-wayland-display (the compositor element). The Quasar fork's `develop` is
# upstream 43d4c25 (gow PR #37) plus the Quasar commits, one per former patch
# file. Bumping this ARG is the deliberate gate that moves the compositor.
GST_WAYLAND_DISPLAY_REPO=https://github.com/salty2011/gst-wayland-display.git
GST_WAYLAND_DISPLAY_REF=310c03eca4b90b653885def4e3348034067c8c72

# Rust toolchain for the compositor + agent builds. cargo-c is pinned to the
# version validated against RUST_VERSION (its MSRV tracks cargo closely).
RUST_VERSION=1.94.0
CARGO_C_VERSION=0.10.23

# rustup's installer. NOT `curl https://sh.rustup.rs | sh`: that URL serves an
# unversioned script, so there is nothing to pin and the bytes piped into a shell
# are whatever the origin returns. These fetch the versioned rustup-init BINARY
# from the archive, which is immutable per version, and check it before running it.
# Both digests agree with the vendor's own published rustup-init.sha256.
# Bumping RUSTUP_VERSION means re-recording both digests.
RUSTUP_VERSION=1.29.0
RUSTUP_INIT_SHA256_X86_64=4acc9acc76d5079515b46346a485974457b5a79893cfb01112423c89aeb5aa10
RUSTUP_INIT_SHA256_AARCH64=9732d6c5e2a098d3521fca8145d826ae0aaa067ef2385ead08e6feac88fa5792

# CUDA toolkit (build) / runtime libs (nv stage). The toolchain is ALWAYS built
# CUDA-enabled so one /opt/gst and one agent binary serve both vendors.
CUDA_PKG_VERSION=13-2

# ── RUNTIME pins (change ⇒ only the ~5 min runtime image is rebuilt) ──────────

# Static docker CLI: the agent launches sibling app containers over the socket.
# This binary drives the MOUNTED HOST DOCKER SOCKET, so a substituted tarball is
# host-level code execution. Docker publishes no checksum beside these tarballs;
# the digests below were recorded from the fetched bytes and freeze them, so a
# later change to a released version's tarball is a build failure, not a silent swap.
DOCKER_VERSION=27.5.1
DOCKER_CLI_SHA256_X86_64=4f798b3ee1e0140eab5bf30b0edc4e84f4cdb53255a429dc3bbae9524845d640
DOCKER_CLI_SHA256_AARCH64=e6b53725a73763ab3f988c73f8772eaed429754c1a579db5ff11f21990fd1817

# Sampling profiler for the never-promoted `profiling` target (PROF-02, #389).
SAMPLY_VERSION=0.13.1
